  'This syllabus is designed for a one-semester Global Health course for health professions, public health, and MPH-adjacent students. It combines disease burden, health systems, governance, equity, and practical program reasoning.',
  $ghjson${"slug": "global-health", "title": "Global Health", "description": "This syllabus is designed for a one-semester Global Health course for health professions, public health, and MPH-adjacent students. It combines disease burden, health systems, governance, equity, and practical program reasoning.", "topics": [{"id": "143b9088-6361-42ce-9b49-66099a725241", "type": "topic", "title": "Course Orientation, Global Health Concepts, and Historical Foundations", "description": "This opening unit defines global health as a field concerned with health improvement, equity, cross-border determinants, and transnational cooperation. Students learn the vocabulary and history needed to interpret later debates.", "children": [{"id": "69daaf3e-fc67-4bd6-8b69-8d26636b5d3c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What Global Health Means", "description": "Students learn how global health differs from international health and public health while overlapping with both.", "children": [{"id": "c1cf0431-fb22-4d98-8eca-40235708a62d", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity, prevention, and transnational determinants"}, {"id": "106c2e8a-4690-49b0-b4c7-b628469b309a", "type": "concept", "title": "Population-level and systems-level thinking"}, {"id": "fde74259-c72a-4909-9b1c-74015b9b302d", "type": "concept", "title": "Interdisciplinary roles and career pathways"}]}, {"id": "db5b2c71-eb7f-4a74-a8fa-8f4ffa84821a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical Foundations", "description": "History helps students see how colonialism, development, philanthropy, and institutions shaped the field.", "children": [{"id": "cdbd129f-4e24-4c28-8c23-f14949d0937a", "type": "concept", "title": "Tropical medicine and colonial legacies"}, {"id": "e4c8a6ab-edce-4a1b-87f0-1ab1b589c8a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary health care and Alma-Ata"}, {"id": "e62a7ee5-a237-4ff8-afaf-d4eb727bcced", "type": "concept", "title": "Global health after HIV/AIDS and COVID-19"}]}, {"id": "45db9e52-3991-4427-aaab-4e9e1c31b957", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core Frameworks", "description": "Students learn recurring frames for analyzing global health problems.", "children": [{"id": "08e9c54d-c32e-4455-9f09-a8dcf475c93c", "type": "concept", "title": "Burden, risk, and vulnerability"}, {"id": "e8515248-17e7-4478-a4c9-6f3b24ab09af", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights-based and capabilities approaches"}, {"id": "7718181b-ea93-4c2b-8af5-e5d3ff13aa7e", "type": "concept", "title": "Social medicine and structural determinants"}]}]}, {"id": "4902906d-6744-46ea-80cb-4fd448364975", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Burden of Disease, Metrics, and Data Literacy", "description": "This unit teaches students how global health problems are measured and compared. It builds comfort with indicators, uncertainty, and responsible use of data.", "children": [{"id": "be282139-63e4-47b7-9fe5-ceba4b38fb48", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Health Indicators", "description": "Students learn common measures used to compare population health.", "children": [{"id": "cc6df6c7-c760-463e-bc3b-30e183a0f1b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Mortality, morbidity, incidence, prevalence"}, {"id": "7c10aa4f-679e-483c-9518-3491afcb49ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Life expectancy and healthy life expectancy"}, {"id": "a382530b-e241-410d-8e1b-92cd220a674b", "type": "concept", "title": "DALYs, QALYs, YLLs, and YLDs"}]}, {"id": "061e3fad-f872-459a-88af-ea1e26b4be81", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Sources and Interpretation", "description": "Students learn where global health data come from and why estimates differ.", "children": [{"id": "5b4af82e-89c3-406d-8429-302612a0145b", "type": "concept", "title": "WHO Global Health Observatory"}, {"id": "f6470184-4a58-4b4d-9dfa-8d244abb9985", "type": "concept", "title": "IHME Global Burden of Disease"}, {"id": "f7a32d40-630e-477e-9e95-22937d620397", "type": "concept", "title": "Surveillance, surveys, registries, and modeled estimates"}]}, {"id": "7e83b188-80d1-4420-966c-86eba33ad34c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Ethics and Limits", "description": "Students learn to ask what data include, exclude, and imply.", "children": [{"id": "c2e33873-ad64-42d8-bdc0-7760bae77cd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement bias and missing data"}, {"id": "e63c44b7-9020-453b-b26e-6a0531c75f40", "type": "concept", "title": "Uncertainty intervals"}, {"id": "06dcd204-9d71-4b12-823c-1320bb3483e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Country comparisons and ecological fallacies"}]}]}, {"id": "6f8c7617-6122-47cd-89f2-7f8f360f7f68", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Determinants, Poverty, Inequality, and Structural Violence", "description": "Global health outcomes are shaped by living conditions, power, and opportunity. This unit teaches students to move beyond individual risk factors toward structural explanation.", "children": [{"id": "de72836f-a3af-44ea-a87e-8ce5323c6edb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social Determinants of Health", "description": "Students learn how social conditions become health outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "8e6ecf55-e263-45eb-8c1f-93d4c2f10e80", "type": "concept", "title": "Income, education, housing, work, food, and environment"}, {"id": "a70337ed-89e2-470a-b186-07e92cfb1f12", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender, race, caste, migration, and disability"}, {"id": "e5bd9755-de68-4eba-a46d-8d58b6d3d148", "type": "concept", "title": "Life-course effects"}]}, {"id": "92b83f6e-c7e0-4203-90c3-32d150f68e84", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Poverty and Development", "description": "Students connect health to economic and social development.", "children": [{"id": "a0e291e4-6c2d-4d04-a001-2947e62257c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute and relative poverty"}, {"id": "6aa68057-7dbd-4d00-ad95-4f8a2531ef3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Human development indicators"}, {"id": "21a1297d-7663-400e-beb8-b78d77bbae15", "type": "concept", "title": "Health-poverty feedback loops"}]}, {"id": "381d3fef-f261-4495-af90-ed42695eb79c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural Violence and Inequity", "description": "Students learn how institutions and histories produce patterned suffering.", "children": [{"id": "0bf87abf-e5c5-4219-8c21-12722bc191d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Colonialism and extraction"}, {"id": "38876a6a-0437-489c-978e-c8188b6752bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Racism and exclusion"}, {"id": "63c2ccb6-d7df-4c7d-ae2c-7c7b10fe5fb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Access, stigma, and social marginalization"}]}]}, {"id": "dc2352b8-fdae-4b15-b1d1-5ae507ac68fd", "type": "topic", "title": "Communicable Diseases, Outbreaks, and Global Health Security", "description": "This unit covers infectious disease as both a biological and systems problem. Students learn transmission, prevention, outbreak response, and the politics of preparedness.", "children": [{"id": "51ad5118-dd3d-43bb-917c-622b8d4b68f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transmission and Control", "description": "Students learn the basic logic of infectious disease spread and interruption.", "children": [{"id": "b2634c75-a3d9-4a45-8eac-54a35fd976c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservoirs, modes of transmission, and R0"}, {"id": "ccd57078-70fc-4e75-b20e-2080447134b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Vaccination, treatment, isolation, and vector control"}, {"id": "80e94f74-1fea-4fd8-b2c5-49c3a6485f34", "type": "concept", "title": "Surveillance and contact tracing"}]}, {"id": "ed99ce61-2f10-4602-8155-0306de91b70c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major Global Infectious Diseases", "description": "Students examine high-burden and high-concern infections.", "children": [{"id": "096eeb44-2313-46ba-aff7-ed254553af9a", "type": "concept", "title": "HIV, tuberculosis, malaria"}, {"id": "85fdba7e-34e1-4fcf-9986-31f1e7f5a4f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Neglected tropical diseases"}, {"id": "3db81bca-0310-47f7-83ff-81c39d16a1f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Emerging and re-emerging infections"}]}, {"id": "2bb97ce7-5fd6-41d8-a19b-607ef239753f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Health Security", "description": "Students learn how countries and institutions prepare for health threats.", "children": [{"id": "2f021cb4-3ec3-4594-adcb-9f3341974b08", "type": "concept", "title": "International Health Regulations"}, {"id": "7aadf4f8-bfaa-4dfa-9585-9ea1ac114e25", "type": "concept", "title": "Pandemic preparedness"}, {"id": "a87a9f9d-c641-4ee6-ad0a-831f0648dee7", "type": "concept", "title": "Laboratory, surveillance, and emergency operations capacity"}]}]}, {"id": "b9892a37-ff5c-4e4c-b2ce-6c7ac377746a", "type": "topic", "title": "Noncommunicable Diseases, Injuries, Mental Health, and Aging", "description": "NCDs and injuries account for much global mortality and disability. This unit shows how chronic disease, mental health, violence, and aging are central global health issues.", "children": [{"id": "0ca676de-0a80-4e98-a774-af5299a175a1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "NCD Burden and Risk Factors", "description": "Students learn the scale and drivers of chronic disease worldwide.", "children": [{"id": "7209df0d-9e7c-40e7-83f4-92d6da2fd96b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cardiovascular disease, cancer, diabetes, chronic respiratory disease"}, {"id": "0399aaff-48df-4e03-b21e-2ac273a50e82", "type": "concept", "title": "Tobacco, alcohol, diet, inactivity, air pollution"}, {"id": "f64aadfb-1f6f-4fa2-b6be-f8efacfeff18", "type": "concept", "title": "Commercial determinants of health"}]}, {"id": "2a17ca84-6338-48fa-a6b5-4111023ffa21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Injuries and Violence", "description": "Students consider preventable injuries as public health problems.", "children": [{"id": "9ee1b277-d2b2-477f-828b-8f82c8a95f1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Road traffic injuries"}, {"id": "2920d31b-dfe2-4da9-91ff-3eefee093922", "type": "concept", "title": "Occupational injury"}, {"id": "a69323bd-125d-4646-9db2-195622cc29af", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpersonal violence and conflict-related harm"}]}, {"id": "69247b17-8332-4121-8f3d-ff2973c807fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mental Health and Aging", "description": "Students learn why disability, stigma, and long-term care matter globally.", "children": [{"id": "3411d355-0b3d-4c96-934c-27870be403d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Depression, anxiety, and severe mental illness"}, {"id": "0ba3ebce-e0d1-4e59-a1a5-e9e025ec9ea7", "type": "concept", "title": "Dementia and aging populations"}, {"id": "0e709236-5232-41d9-a70c-c34f3b8ecf56", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration into primary care"}]}]}, {"id": "d95e58d0-044f-4189-ba68-e4e9c5100862", "type": "topic", "title": "Maternal, Newborn, Child, and Adolescent Health", "description": "This unit focuses on health across early life and reproductive years. Students learn interventions that reduce preventable mortality and improve lifelong wellbeing.", "children": [{"id": "df27847b-0d90-43f5-9f02-1a3e3a106c7e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Maternal and Reproductive Health", "description": "Students learn the determinants of safe pregnancy, childbirth, and reproductive autonomy.", "children": [{"id": "3f4ecda1-a283-42a3-a767-9328750ca932", "type": "concept", "title": "Antenatal, delivery, and postpartum care"}, {"id": "de3b790d-5006-44f1-a716-6126843d4cc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Family planning and reproductive rights"}, {"id": "77b0867d-2c4c-44d1-ac0e-2eb2f9acbc4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Maternal mortality and respectful care"}]}, {"id": "2df83eac-d978-4864-bdf4-8714003ef2ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Newborn and Child Health", "description": "Students examine the major causes and prevention of child mortality.", "children": [{"id": "c3a3e538-d603-48d0-893c-5f58f6f7d48c", "type": "concept", "title": "Neonatal complications"}, {"id": "d4ccf205-65a9-41df-a2d4-0050f7efa414", "type": "concept", "title": "Immunization and integrated management of childhood illness"}, {"id": "6e358501-67e9-48ca-981d-7d1b68320a3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Growth, development, and early childhood interventions"}]}, {"id": "2af819cf-e0c7-407d-bc48-097b42d8ca7e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Adolescent Health", "description": "Students learn why adolescence is a critical window for prevention and empowerment.", "children": [{"id": "639e82c2-96e2-4347-8d59-c67cafc20ef0", "type": "concept", "title": "Sexual and reproductive health"}, {"id": "2299b2ab-48ee-4547-a89b-4372806cc92f", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental health and violence prevention"}, {"id": "8a668eb8-a7fa-4055-b3d5-854ccc02e2fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Education, gender equity, and youth participation"}]}]}, {"id": "bfea73ce-c467-42fe-a79d-f11ec533683f", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition, Water, Sanitation, and Environmental Health", "description": "Basic conditions such as food, water, sanitation, and environment shape health at population scale. This unit connects household-level risks to systems and infrastructure.", "children": [{"id": "c2cb835d-3b08-4f1a-b02c-026de6223922", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nutrition and Food Security", "description": "Students learn forms of malnutrition and their causes.", "children": [{"id": "40f07abe-2f76-4215-b4a7-0688a7a63fb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Undernutrition, micronutrient deficiency, overweight, and obesity"}, {"id": "5232600f-fc50-4d87-8312-81e3a69ffa19", "type": "concept", "title": "Food systems and affordability"}, {"id": "33095e6f-547c-41bb-946e-bb9c62672e88", "type": "concept", "title": "Nutrition-sensitive interventions"}]}, {"id": "d211a8f4-9502-4151-aebb-714fc318f44d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene", "description": "Students learn why WASH is central to disease prevention and dignity.", "children": [{"id": "28f34bdb-4d69-4956-b808-30cdc2e898df", "type": "concept", "title": "Safe water supply"}, {"id": "83468584-b046-48fc-a0dc-ddc48c7d6d63", "type": "concept", "title": "Sanitation and wastewater"}, {"id": "9a857db2-c885-499e-819f-03a953aca9a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Hygiene behavior and infrastructure"}]}, {"id": "a38991c3-c982-4885-a0a2-ec335259cf97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Environmental Health Risks", "description": "Students connect environmental exposure to global disease burden.", "children": [{"id": "61a411d0-e887-4de4-9ff1-a68a8e8aebf9", "type": "concept", "title": "Household and ambient air pollution"}, {"id": "b98a802a-ce98-483a-bb6e-758b42431ddb", "type": "concept", "title": "Toxic exposures"}, {"id": "f4b37de6-1138-4984-88cd-4f8d0b2b7dce", "type": "concept", "title": "Urbanization and occupational risks"}]}]}, {"id": "4cbb8f43-7eff-44d4-9bdc-b3c0ee5f79a5", "type": "topic", "title": "Health Systems in LMICs and Comparative Health Systems", "description": "Health systems determine whether effective interventions reach people. This unit teaches students to analyze system building blocks, access, quality, and financing.", "children": [{"id": "19eb7a9c-c434-47f6-9ff2-ff960f789c37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Health System Building Blocks", "description": "Students learn a framework for diagnosing system performance.", "children": [{"id": "dca3c141-e0f2-4b4e-8615-2f27b5dfd780", "type": "concept", "title": "Service delivery and workforce"}, {"id": "92478d0b-9d86-4092-a1fa-a5d855e3d7d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Medicines, technologies, and information systems"}, {"id": "97ef2a08-a5bb-43aa-8162-fa292d1c99cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance and financing"}]}, {"id": "52795724-9675-40de-b13f-071efbf6efeb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Primary Health Care and Universal Health Coverage", "description": "Students examine approaches to equitable access.", "children": [{"id": "86789796-9ce8-4d89-8ddc-f364cf79c3d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary care platforms"}, {"id": "1cb1c94f-ee9e-4ab2-b745-0bad4f4852c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal health coverage"}, {"id": "3462ad75-6bf6-4926-85cc-8dc1e0a1965b", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality, affordability, and financial protection"}]}, {"id": "3ed13bea-dc07-4c5f-9801-c03af9d37750", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative Health Systems", "description": "Students learn to compare systems without assuming one model fits all.", "children": [{"id": "e764b8d0-5e3d-40b5-83da-41704f83fc57", "type": "concept", "title": "Public, private, and mixed systems"}, {"id": "1a0e1b9b-75e7-4d6d-83e6-0e3be84d3c75", "type": "concept", "title": "Decentralization and referral networks"}, {"id": "3d19c69b-8349-46e0-9250-e981d8375760", "type": "concept", "title": "Community health workers and task sharing"}]}]}, {"id": "19111d8d-1fe7-4f28-a2a9-753bc1e59708", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Health Governance, Actors, Law, and Financing", "description": "Global health is shaped by institutions, funding, treaties, and power. This unit helps students map actors and understand how priorities are set.", "children": [{"id": "bc02d825-f750-4eb4-94d3-db606988ef0b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Health Actors", "description": "Students learn who does global health and how authority is distributed.", "children": [{"id": "896cca21-c3d8-41e0-be3a-c294811238b6", "type": "concept", "title": "WHO, UNICEF, World Bank, bilateral donors"}, {"id": "90e1861c-ff6d-49ae-bc45-b33854d14779", "type": "concept", "title": "NGOs, foundations, private sector, and civil society"}, {"id": "d1405d57-0657-4e8f-8052-490b8ef8d420", "type": "concept", "title": "National ministries and local organizations"}]}, {"id": "d6dcb6f8-5366-4f83-ae49-f115ae7b48a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Governance and Law", "description": "Students learn how rules and norms shape cooperation.", "children": [{"id": "2f611e73-cbb1-4110-b94c-bca5207c5fd5", "type": "concept", "title": "International Health Regulations"}, {"id": "e92dbb95-2fec-4627-a31d-44927bbeaee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Global health law and human rights"}, {"id": "3d07f208-e87f-4a62-a355-d19dd805eaf2", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability and legitimacy"}]}, {"id": "9efc4aed-e7f1-45fd-8bff-0b5e85f3e429", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financing and Priority Setting", "description": "Students learn how money influences what gets done.", "children": [{"id": "18dd3c66-b4f9-4762-baee-3bef0bc43bd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Donor funding and domestic financing"}, {"id": "266bff02-d225-4f4c-90dc-63a514997fd9", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-effectiveness and allocative decisions"}, {"id": "dcda7cf0-0fcd-4e62-8f45-5f7dfd0e6385", "type": "concept", "title": "Vertical versus horizontal funding"}]}]}, {"id": "8909a45e-4bc0-4226-b67d-c6d05b968800", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Health Programs, Implementation, and Evaluation", "description": "Good ideas do not automatically become effective programs. This unit teaches implementation thinking, evaluation, and adaptation to context.", "children": [{"id": "27ae74e0-40d6-446b-94b5-7d77686a1977", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Program Design", "description": "Students learn how interventions connect problems, activities, and outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "f560b458-4a31-4f45-8207-7a55c237043d", "type": "concept", "title": "Needs assessment"}, {"id": "8cfb57e7-b8e6-4408-89e3-e824350da5d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory of change and logic models"}, {"id": "2786862c-a29a-449c-8490-f42615f9a738", "type": "concept", "title": "Community engagement and co-design"}]}, {"id": "f517aee8-3d0e-47ad-9b0b-26f241177fdc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implementation Science", "description": "Students learn why delivery fails and how programs can adapt.", "children": [{"id": "2f0fc41d-b0d4-4b7e-a1d3-4e3e89b94064", "type": "concept", "title": "Fidelity and adaptation"}, {"id": "6c277306-24c0-491f-a34d-c8349a3bd083", "type": "concept", "title": "Barriers and facilitators"}, {"id": "53f4b517-f813-4ca2-866d-d14df432fa8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale-up and sustainability"}]}, {"id": "62684adb-040f-476c-9856-4ea6ee17b2a3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation", "description": "Students learn how to judge whether programs work and for whom.", "children": [{"id": "f3b12604-0625-4c60-9ce6-7c6ff270f8aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Process, outcome, and impact evaluation"}, {"id": "e01925a8-c2a9-426c-81dd-f2e00c9fdd2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Indicators and data collection"}, {"id": "379529e5-c233-4187-914d-cb400b35120e", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity-focused evaluation"}]}]}, {"id": "97fe1c2a-cd93-4a4b-bce9-79c11f6c8b96", "type": "topic", "title": "Humanitarian Emergencies, Displacement, and Disaster Response", "description": "Conflict, disasters, and forced migration create urgent health needs and complex ethical choices. Students learn core response principles and health priorities.", "children": [{"id": "d1d97aab-c5a7-4bf1-a520-e02340fa9d81", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Humanitarian Health Priorities", "description": "Students learn the immediate health needs in crisis settings.", "children": [{"id": "30548601-1946-4ceb-92a8-27cbd006ef1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Shelter, water, sanitation, nutrition, and primary care"}, {"id": "cc8d5b1f-c85e-4df4-af68-1e23ce65bbef", "type": "concept", "title": "Communicable disease prevention"}, {"id": "fd53bab7-ff33-4dcd-873c-e9fbfc3bc10b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental health and psychosocial support"}]}, {"id": "4a522764-92cd-4a57-a72d-0f2110482376", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forced Migration and Refugee Health", "description": "Students examine health across displacement journeys.", "children": [{"id": "94e9ea60-9e5a-4ea6-8cb1-83e10e6cc7d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Refugees, asylum seekers, internally displaced persons"}, {"id": "cbb3c08e-9a73-4423-8ad0-524b07ed414d", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity of care"}, {"id": "0dc6bb2b-78c5-4444-a9ee-576324b0bbe9", "type": "concept", "title": "Legal status, access, and protection"}]}, {"id": "9e6eaf34-383c-47ea-aeed-9ae8c963ae84", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Humanitarian Coordination and Ethics", "description": "Students learn how agencies coordinate under pressure.", "children": [{"id": "929b4c15-6248-4857-944a-c9dd3602cc45", "type": "concept", "title": "Cluster system overview"}, {"id": "018172ab-4d32-437a-93ed-1c3e693a477c", "type": "concept", "title": "Do no harm and neutrality debates"}, {"id": "edad1136-7232-4323-b4f3-1d66035b1b27", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability to affected populations"}]}]}, {"id": "731f12c3-6b7a-4b53-b140-c35cc1057bf9", "type": "topic", "title": "Planetary Health, Climate Change, and One Health", "description": "Human health depends on ecological systems. This unit connects climate, biodiversity, animals, food systems, and environmental change to disease and wellbeing.", "children": [{"id": "ec31e910-5bec-4187-8995-4ae19fc234dc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Climate Change and Health", "description": "Students learn major climate-related pathways to illness.", "children": [{"id": "18717984-66ee-4a37-8b40-f4aa6c5ab585", "type": "concept", "title": "Heat, extreme weather, air quality"}, {"id": "bb5f239d-69dc-473d-af57-77b0ba5c9daf", "type": "concept", "title": "Food and water security"}, {"id": "77d29144-e512-4de7-9b3f-cc3156402f72", "type": "concept", "title": "Climate migration and mental health"}]}, {"id": "ae0b5cd4-c034-4720-878b-892d6027dadb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "One Health", "description": "Students learn why human, animal, and environmental health are linked.", "children": [{"id": "73f64e60-5b1e-423d-806e-dc718e66da27", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoonotic spillover"}, {"id": "0addf791-1958-4248-a8a9-25a4fe006c31", "type": "concept", "title": "Antimicrobial resistance"}, {"id": "5fe843e4-ec0c-4d5d-be10-5a5cdc574f66", "type": "concept", "title": "Veterinary, ecological, and public health collaboration"}]}, {"id": "814d1bf9-2739-452b-8011-9970e387fde6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planetary Health Interventions", "description": "Students consider health co-benefits of environmental action.", "children": [{"id": "8b7fe114-247a-455d-a37b-2a0e70ac93d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Mitigation and adaptation"}, {"id": "883b5b5e-0156-4bef-b9ba-3e38c887d95c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sustainable food systems"}, {"id": "380040e3-94ab-414d-9acd-2cdf4eb8d4ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban planning and resilient infrastructure"}]}]}, {"id": "a06a4cd6-8149-4fc8-87e0-cfdb705385bd", "type": "topic", "title": "Global Health Ethics, Equity, and Decolonizing Global Health", "description": "This unit examines who benefits, who decides, and whose knowledge counts. Students learn to identify ethical tensions and equity-centered alternatives.", "children": [{"id": "6aa5b654-c27c-44a1-a835-7fc2211c1556", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Health Ethics", "description": "Students learn ethical frameworks for research, programs, and partnerships.", "children": [{"id": "49f13c65-7232-41ef-b4c9-e5521b28d7f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Beneficence, justice, autonomy, and solidarity"}, {"id": "cf4b469f-1ee8-4ff2-a9d6-03c5fe176e48", "type": "concept", "title": "Research ethics and informed consent"}, {"id": "bda02be4-2407-4edc-a14d-2d3c7045dea3", "type": "concept", "title": "Resource allocation and priority setting"}]}, {"id": "f4ca48db-4c8b-4c4f-ad6d-fa6a5c6a8fe9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity and Power", "description": "Students analyze inequity in institutions and knowledge production.", "children": [{"id": "77565b75-c99f-4e16-a248-ee7565b6473a", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and authorship"}, {"id": "eb6b7f9e-c20a-4221-a8fd-5335e6bfe1ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Partnership asymmetry"}, {"id": "3c438bce-84c6-4dbe-816f-a4b18456158b", "type": "concept", "title": "Funding, agenda setting, and expertise"}]}, {"id": "2e424609-8356-4a05-8a2c-bdd770f5be0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Decolonizing Global Health", "description": "Students engage current debates about transforming practice.", "children": [{"id": "656668f0-953b-45f3-926e-7a39fd9dacb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Local leadership and ownership"}, {"id": "a7b82617-af13-412b-93a6-f76a47e8e38c", "type": "concept", "title": "Language and narrative framing"}, {"id": "b085e74c-ad8e-48e7-a8b1-59f850138284", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability, reciprocity, and reparative approaches"}]}]}, {"id": "b6027abf-fa7f-4639-8b4c-8b0e4c432eec", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Global Health Case Analysis and Applied Practice", "description": "The final unit asks students to synthesize course tools through cases. Students practice moving from problem description to context-aware recommendations.", "children": [{"id": "6a3a83ee-d628-4d7e-8351-d8061a4adda8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case Analysis Method", "description": "Students learn a structured approach to global health cases.", "children": [{"id": "323b1d66-9dae-4384-a95b-13b1074a9e3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Define the problem and stakeholders"}, {"id": "6b76d293-af67-4884-8a79-6d95f67bfe0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Use data and context"}, {"id": "538897d7-494f-464d-a046-99cf0b07d13b", "type": "concept", "title": "Identify tradeoffs and uncertainties"}]}, {"id": "8827fe61-d120-4482-9dd8-1bf2a3618b2d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy and Program Recommendations", "description": "Students practice making feasible, ethical recommendations.", "children": [{"id": "12638238-100f-42cd-83a9-e465088a0030", "type": "concept", "title": "Intervention options"}, {"id": "6043f62d-c3a8-4fbb-af72-2c6958a0ace7", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation constraints"}, {"id": "8db099bc-df33-40ec-866e-6b7ba8eec15a", "type": "concept", "title": "Monitoring and evaluation plan"}]}, {"id": "e1c4c1c9-ec4a-426f-8d7e-7df6acab8fd7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional Practice and Reflection", "description": "Students connect the course to careers and responsibilities.", "children": [{"id": "2eb9e7ad-8d42-4687-9a5b-9ac6aca92a27", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural humility"}, {"id": "7e1cc285-7d81-4457-a6a2-4ccdc66501d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Interdisciplinary collaboration"}, {"id": "55756218-2ce9-4d65-b1b9-353512592acc", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal role, limits, and learning agenda"}]}]}], "dbBacked": true}$ghjson$::jsonb,
